# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# RAW FINANCIAL DATA — NEVER COMMIT
#
# These hold bank exports and statement PDFs containing full name, home
# address and partial card numbers. They stay on this machine only.
#
# The .githooks/pre-commit hook enforces this independently of this file, and
# also scans staged content for identifiers. Install it with:
#     git config core.hooksPath .githooks
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Every raw export and statement lives under these two directories, so the
# directory rules are what does the work. A blanket *.csv rule is deliberately
# NOT used — it would also exclude the sanitised outputs in docs/ that belong
# in the repo. The pre-commit hook scans content, which catches a CSV carrying
# identifiers far more reliably than an extension ever could.
raw/
derived/
*.pdf
statements/
statements-*/

# Local machine-specific config (account numbers used by the scripts)
scripts/local-config.json
docs/connectivity/provider-account-map.local.json

# Secrets — these live in Render environment variables and nowhere else
.env
.env.*
*.local
secrets.json

# Node
node_modules/
npm-debug.log*
.npm/

# OS / editor
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
